{% doc %}
  Voucher (discount code) row for the cart drawer footer summary.

  Renders as ONE compact row inside .cart-footer-summary that morphs in place
  between three states — idle trigger → open input → applied chip — instead of
  adding a new module to an already dense drawer.

  Server state is derived from cart.cart_level_discount_applications filtered to
  type == 'discount_code' (automatic discounts live in the same array and must
  not be shown as a removable voucher). Liquid has no cart.discount_codes.

  The Ajax layer in MiniCart.liquid mirrors this exact markup client-side after
  POST /cart/update.js so the optimistic render and the server render agree.

  @example
  {% render 'CartVoucher' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign voucher_codes = ''
  assign voucher_amount = 0
  for d in cart.cart_level_discount_applications
    if d.type == 'discount_code'
      assign voucher_codes = voucher_codes | append: d.title | append: ','
      assign voucher_amount = voucher_amount | plus: d.total_allocated_amount
    endif
  endfor
  assign voucher_list = voucher_codes | split: ','

  assign voucher_state = 'idle'
  if voucher_list.size > 0
    assign voucher_state = 'applied'
  endif
-%}

<div class="cart-voucher" data-cart-voucher data-state="{{ voucher_state }}">
  <button
    type="button"
    class="cart-voucher-trigger"
    data-voucher-open
    aria-expanded="false"
    aria-controls="cart-voucher-panel"
  >
    <span class="cart-voucher-trigger-label">
      <svg class="cart-voucher-icon" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M8.4 1.7 14.3 7.6a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.4l-5.3 5.3a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0L1.7 8.4a1 1 0 0 1-.3-.7V2.4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5.3a1 1 0 0 1 .7.3Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <circle cx="4.9" cy="4.9" r="1.05" fill="currentColor"/>
      </svg>
      {{ 'cart.voucher.trigger' | t }}
    </span>
    <span class="cart-voucher-trigger-cta">{{ 'cart.voucher.trigger_cta' | t }}</span>
  </button>

  <div class="cart-voucher-panel" id="cart-voucher-panel">
    <div class="cart-voucher-panel-inner">
      <label class="cart-voucher-label" for="cart-voucher-input">{{ 'cart.voucher.label' | t }}</label>
      <div class="cart-voucher-field">
        <input
          id="cart-voucher-input"
          class="cart-voucher-input"
          type="text"
          inputmode="text"
          autocomplete="off"
          autocapitalize="characters"
          autocorrect="off"
          spellcheck="false"
          enterkeyhint="done"
          maxlength="64"
          placeholder="{{ 'cart.voucher.placeholder' | t }}"
          data-voucher-input
        >
        <button type="button" class="cart-voucher-submit" data-voucher-submit>
          <span class="cart-voucher-submit-label">{{ 'cart.voucher.submit' | t }}</span>
          <span class="cart-voucher-submit-busy" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg class="cart-voucher-spinner" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" opacity=".25"/>
              <path d="M12 3a9 9 0 0 1 9 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        {%- comment -%}
          Escape alone was the only way out, which is no way out at all on a
          touch screen.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="cart-voucher-cancel"
          data-voucher-cancel
          aria-label="{{ 'cart.voucher.cancel' | t }}"
        >
          <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M1 1 11 11M11 1 1 11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Several codes can be live at once, but only across discount CLASSES that
    Shopify is configured to combine — an order discount stacks with a shipping
    discount, two order discounts do not. Verified on this store:
      MOR10,FREESHIPPING -> both applicable:true
      MOR10,HABIT10      -> MOR10 flips to applicable:false
    The second case is why the JS compares the applied set before and after:
    a non-combinable code silently evicts the one already on the cart.

    This server render is a best-effort starting point, not the full set.
    cart_level_discount_applications only holds MERCHANDISE discounts, and
    Liquid has no cart.discount_codes — so a free-shipping code is invisible
    here and renders no chip until refreshCartUI runs on open and syncVoucherUI
    rebuilds the row from cart.discount_codes, which does list it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="cart-voucher-applied">
    <span class="cart-voucher-chips" data-voucher-chips>
      {%- for code in voucher_list -%}
        <span class="cart-voucher-chip" data-voucher-chip="{{ code | escape }}">
          <svg width="11" height="9" viewBox="0 0 14 11" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M1 5.5 5 9.5 13 1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="cart-voucher-code">{{ code }}</span>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="cart-voucher-remove"
            data-voucher-remove="{{ code | escape }}"
            aria-label="{{ 'cart.voucher.remove' | t }} {{ code }}"
          >
            <svg width="9" height="9" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M1 1 11 11M11 1 1 11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
        </span>
      {%- endfor -%}
      <button type="button" class="cart-voucher-addmore" data-voucher-open>
        + {{ 'cart.voucher.add_more' | t }}
      </button>
    </span>
    <span class="cart-voucher-amount" data-voucher-amount>
      {%- if voucher_amount > 0 -%}
        −{{ voucher_amount | money }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'cart.voucher.applied_at_checkout' | t }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Deliberately a sibling of the panel, not a child: it has to stay readable
    in the applied state too (e.g. "voucher applied, but you dropped below the
    free-shipping threshold"), and a live region that gets collapsed away mid
    announcement is skipped by most screen readers. aria-atomic re-reads the
    whole node so iOS VoiceOver still speaks a repeated identical error.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p
    class="cart-voucher-msg"
    data-voucher-msg
    role="status"
    aria-live="polite"
    aria-atomic="true"
  ></p>
</div>
